[Music]  [Music]  hello there  general i didn't have a whole lot of  time to make a big production video this  weekend  given the fact that i'm still playing  the game as well as some other projects  i have to take care of as well but i  still wanted to present  something to hold you over until i get  around to the bigger stuff  so here's a smaller video covering some  of my findings during my playthrough of  age of calamity so far  this includes little bits of lore  secrets or any other things i found  interesting or peculiar  so let's get started  [Music]  one thing that has eluded us in the  backstory of breath the wild is how  exactly the guardians were found  in one of the first cutscenes of the  game told to us by king rome's spirit we  see some chica researchers digging in  gerudo canyon  after which it shows divine beast vana  boris being discovered embedded in the  sandstone  moments later we see more scientists  standing amidst a group of guardian  stalkers which they dug up as well  however rome never specifies where  exactly these were found  i think most of us assumed that they  were found underneath hyrule castle  since in one of the underground chambers  we find small groups of these machines  still half buried however age of  calamity gives us more insight into some  of the locations the guardians were  discovered as well as the sheer number  of them  apparently the biggest sites of these  excavations were the breach of demise  and the area surrounding oculus citadel  and yes according to the game it's  actually pronounced  accola not akala as many of us assumed  the game shows us just how large these  excavation projects really were  and even how they were dug up upon  discovery they used wooden cranes and  pulleys to extract them from the ground  after which they were likely transported  to either hyrule castle or the royal  ancient tech lab  another interesting detail regarding the  excavations of the relics is that we  finally have confirmation that the  stalkers  were not the only type of guardians  being dug up i actually missed this  during my playthrough of the demo  in the second story mission which takes  place inside the breach of demise  we can find recently dug up guardian sky  watchers  this is a great piece of exhibition  since before age of calamity it has  always been  unclear where exactly the sky watchers  and other guardian types came from  and i think most of us speculated that  they were stored inside the giant column  surrounding hyrule castle  while theorizing about these rumored  columns zelda mentions in her research  notes that these giants may hold even  more guardian types  this made a lot of us assume that they  probably didn't dig up  any of the other types of guardians just  the stalkers  and that the rest emerged from the  columns later but nope they  actually did find other types as well  zelda may have just been speculating  that there were even more types aside  from the ones they already found  this next one is a very minor detail and  i think plenty of you  already figured this one out on your own  during the first mission on death  mountain we eventually come across  the goron hot springs the rook suggests  that we should rest our wary bones here  for a while  if you step into the water of the hot  springs your hearts will replenish one  by one the longer you stay inside  it works exactly the same as it did in  breath of the wild  here too when you stand inside the warm  waters of the hot spring  the same thing happens i think it's nice  to see that they carried this mechanic  over  a little detail that helps tie the games  together  another significant revelation is that  the hylians  due to the efforts of the chica no doubt  actually had access to  portable ancient furnaces the game  refers to them as  simple furnaces and their design  strongly resembles that of the larger  ancient furnaces found in the cluda and  akala  i mean akula this is gonna get some  getting used to  anyway this is a neat little detail it's  obvious that the ancient furnaces were  not built by the modern day chica but  rather discovered and unearthed just  like the other relics so those are the  handiwork of the ancient chica from ten  thousand years ago  the modern-day sheikah likely copied its  design and created small portable  versions of these furnaces  this way they would have access to  ancient energy anywhere they deployed  them  i really like this idea a lot and it  shows just how resourceful the chica  were  copying the designs of their distant  ancestors and turning them into  something new  it's also worth mentioning that aside  from the fact that hyrule castle and the  royal ancient tech lab were the heart of  the sheikah  research the game reveals that these  were not the only locations where  research was conducted  all throughout the breach of the mice  and close to akla citadel we can find  smaller temporary labs  these house all kinds of notes formulas  written on chalkboards  guardian parts and in some cases these  portable furnaces  we also see that some guardians after  being dug up were assembled cleaned and  made operational directly on site  zelda even mentions in one instance in  front of the citadel  that this place used to have a research  lab indicating that these labs were set  up and then dismantled again once the  research was concluded  the queen of hyrule who is said to have  died unexpectedly when zelda was around  the age of 6  has been a subject of debate and mystery  ever since breath the wild  she is spoken about in zelda and king  rome's diaries and is also mentioned  briefly on certain pages in masterworks  but her actual appearance has always  eluded us  in breath of the wild's hyrule castle  more specifically in king rome's secret  room where his diary is  we find a picture ripped from its frame  now some of us speculated that this  might have been a picture of rome and  his wife  we can actually visit this area in age  of calamity as well  and nope it's just a picture of a  landscape  well played nintendo now here's where i  have to show you something from the late  game but don't worry i only show a still  frame and i've removed any other  contacts from the image so it doesn't  really spoil anything in regards to the  main story itself  still if you want to be surprised you  can skip to the time code presented at  the bottom of the screen  alright 3 2 1 ready set go  darth vader is luke's father also  during zelda's last memory from when she  was a child she calls out to her mother  and then she turns around we are then  presented with  this the first time we actually see  zelda's mother in the flesh  but of course in true nintendo fashion  we never see her actual face  right as the camera is about to face her  the screen dips to white  the only thing we can really derive from  this is that she's wearing the same  clothing  zelda is seen wearing in some of the  memories from breath of the wild  as well as some cut scenes in age of  calamity this is the getup she garnishes  mainly when she's present at hyrule  castle or during any formal event  nice to know but still doesn't really  reveal much about the queen  unfortunately but there is one location  where we actually get  another tip of the veil regarding  hyrule's late queen  ever since breath of the wild there's  one important area  inside hyrule castle that has been  hidden from us this room is described  and even depicted in masterworks as  the great hall of which its entrance has  collapsed  due to the events of the calamity thus  making it inaccessible in the actual  game  well in age of calamity we actually get  to visit this location as well  and it's great to see this place finally  realized in game  a grand chapel-like interior decorated  with arches  fire pits statues of knights and draped  with banners depicting the famous crest  of the triforce in loftwing also found  on the hylian shield  more interestingly however in the very  back of the hall we find a statue of two  figures  a man and a woman the man is undoubtedly  king rome himself in his younger years  before he became a football this is  given away by the hair  the clothing as well as the pose of the  statue so by that definition that would  make the figure standing next to him  his wife the queen of hyrule aka zelda's  mother  making this the first and only full  depiction of her  of course the statue itself is still  relatively low poly  and the lighting doesn't exactly help to  see any finer details  but it's still nice that they actually  included this in the game  when i showed this picture to conrad of  the commonwealth realm he noted that the  statue is likely a memorial to their  wedding  and the pose the queen strikes also  looks familiar  it's something we've seen all throughout  the zelda series which usually has some  kind of connection to the divine  whether being to the goddess hylia or  the three golden goddesses who created  the world  praying to them and requesting their  support or showing your devotion to them  in some way  this hints that zelda's mom did have a  connection to the gods the divine or  maybe even the sacred realm in some way  after all  i'm saying after all because this isn't  something we've known for sure  this last one is more of a funny little  detail in breath of the wild  link wasn't exactly the most fleshed out  character partly due to the fact that he  had amnesia  and even the memories we can unlock that  feature him don't really show a whole  lot more than the fact that he was  zelda's knight and that he was  brave and always silent we do see that  he had a friendship with the rook and  mifa the latter of which may have been a  possible romantic relationship in some  shape or form  and of course his relationship to zelda  which started out rocky but then slowly  grew into something more close  but again it doesn't really show much  beyond this in terms of his character  traits  however in her diary zelda does reveal  some little details about him  one of these revelations is that link is  apparently quite a glutton and that he  cannot resist a delicious meal  so it's nice that they actually depict  this in age of calamity on two different  occasions  i mean with the exception of the wind  waker link has generally always been  kind of a blank slate since we're  supposed to project ourselves onto him  but it's nice to see that they actually  show this part of his personality  it just makes him feel more like a real  person despite the fact that he doesn't  speak  and that is all for now i hope to start  creating some bigger theories very soon  but for now i'm mostly gonna  focus on the experience of the game and  not rush through it i really enjoy all  these little backstories and lore  exposition  so i definitely don't wanna skip over  anything a shout out goes to walters  equal  a new member who i forgot to mention in  my last video and ira who recently  joined my patreon  and of course a big thanks to all of you  who support and watch my videos  i will see you all in the next one this  is dawn signing off and  have a good one  [Music]  you

